{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/1421531-\u00e6on-fun-hard-sci-fi-strategy-that-i-know-a-player-will-want-to-use","id":1421531,"title":"[\u00c6on] Fun hard sci-fi strategy that I know a player will want to use","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","The Trinity Continuum","Trinity Continuum: \u00c6on"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-11-02T17:39:11-08:00","id":1421531,"title":"[\u00c6on] Fun hard sci-fi strategy that I know a player will want to use","content":"So if my Leviathan is traveling at speed 6, aimed at the cololition ark, that is also traveling at speed six. If they fire railguns would the speed scale stack for damage?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2421-cknight","name":"cKnight","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"47"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-02T17:53:53-08:00","id":1421534,"title":"","content":"In the Distant Worlds book they mention a similar attack on ivdel","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2421-cknight","name":"cKnight","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"47"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-02T18:00:45-08:00","id":1421535,"title":"","content":"Yes, if they are going against each other, but the targeting difficulty should be proportionally higher. There are a much smaller error margin and firing window with the relativistic time distortions on both sides and everything. BTW, aiming visually is an exercise in futility, near lightspeed everything will be distorted with crazy doppler effect and relativistic shenanigans.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1524-pcontop","name":"pcontop","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1524_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"278"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-02T18:01:00-08:00","id":1421536,"title":"","content":"Yes, but scale don\u2019t stack that way.<br /> <br /> Each scale is several times the lower one, so the rail gun bullet is going at speed 7, plus the scale 6 plus the scale 6 it is 7 + something much lower that is not enough to stack to 8.<br /> <br /> For example, let\u2019s say speed 6 is 1, scale 7 is 5 and scale 8 is 25, so 5 + 1 + 1 = 7 that is far les than 25.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-02T18:08:53-08:00","id":1421537,"title":"","content":"Thanks for the replies. I am thinking of a clear in an aries pod providing targeting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2421-cknight","name":"cKnight","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"47"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-02T18:20:29-08:00","id":1421538,"title":"","content":"I don't think I get your explanation.<br /> <br /> Ship fires at speed 6. Weapon enhancement is already modded by ship size. Target vessel is approaching at speed six. <br /> The difference in speed should be 12.?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2421-cknight","name":"cKnight","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"47"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-02T18:23:14-08:00","id":1421540,"title":"","content":"Speed Scale 12 is WAY more than 2x Speed Scale 6. It's more like 1000x or more. So, I would either add 1 or 0 scale to the inflict injury stunt due to scale with a corresponding complication to the attack roll.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8719-florin","name":"Florin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"940"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-02T18:24:31-08:00","id":1421541,"title":"","content":"Example: ship chasing target, speed 5 vs speed 6, equals a - 1 scale ( 2 enhancement for damage). Or is my thought process and understanding of mechanics wrong?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2421-cknight","name":"cKnight","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"47"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-02T18:37:34-08:00","id":1421542,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>cKnight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/1421531-\u00e6on-fun-hard-sci-fi-strategy-that-i-know-a-player-will-want-to-use?p=1421541#post1421541\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Example: ship chasing target, speed 5 vs speed 6, equals a - 1 scale ( 2 enhancement for damage). Or is my thought process and understanding of mechanics wrong?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I kind of want to know myself as this is how I had been doing it. Units at radically different scales (ship at 6 and human at 1) don't even need rolls. Units at near scales (human at 1 and cheeta at 3) interact with penalty. Ship 1 at scale 20 vs ship 2 at scale 20 operate as if there is no scale at all mechanically. Ship at 6 and ship at 7 cause the lower ship to take a penalty. <br /> <br /> Whether narratively this is ships going ten million miles per our or the speed of purple doesn't matter. <br /> <br /> At least that s how I thought of it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-02T18:41:56-08:00","id":1421543,"title":"","content":"That's kind of my point. Two ships traveling at reletvistic speeds towards one another and a shot is fired.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2421-cknight","name":"cKnight","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"47"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-02T18:45:45-08:00","id":1421544,"title":"","content":"I know this thought is more technical than the rules but my player reads lot of hard sci-fi ,<br /> where velocity energy matters in space combat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2421-cknight","name":"cKnight","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"47"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-02T18:50:52-08:00","id":1421545,"title":"","content":"I get that scale shouldn't be added strait out but, but storyguide wise how much should I add to enhancements for damage?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2421-cknight","name":"cKnight","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"47"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-02T18:56:13-08:00","id":1421546,"title":"","content":"Just for reference&quot; Star Carrier&quot; in this series of books first strikes at near light speed usually decide battles","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2421-cknight","name":"cKnight","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"47"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-02T19:20:56-08:00","id":1421550,"title":"","content":"Scale is not linear progression, it\u2019s a exponential progression, scale 1 is about 15km/h scale 2 is about 75km/h, and so on.<br /> <br /> Let\u2019s say scale 6 speed is about 10Mm/h, and scale 7 is about 40Mm/h and scale 8 is about 160Mm/h.<br /> The ships are moving at speed 6 one against the other, and the bullet is fired at speed 7.<br /> So the speed the bullet is moving is about 40Mm/h above the 10Mm/h from the ship, and so about 60Mm/h against the approaching ship.<br /> 60Mm/h is almost as close to 160Mm/h as 40Mm/h, so it\u2019s considered at speed 7 yet, and so not worth of extra scale in the impact.<br /> <br /> The numbers are not those, but the steps are about that (or an even larger difference).<br /> <br /> Edit: the reference is good, but the impact would be more like a surprise attack at maximum range and less about the extra speed, as the ships are not reducing speed fast enough to change from one round to the other.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":24985,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","user":"Mateus Luz","date":". 11-02-2020, 10:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-03T13:17:08-08:00","id":1421668,"title":"","content":"It seems to me this is a moot point. If both ships are moving at speed 6 then neither has scale on the other. Thus it would not impact the roll as there is no difference in scale.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6-slagheap","name":"Slagheap","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"188"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-03T13:27:56-08:00","id":1421671,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>cKnight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/1421531-\u00e6on-fun-hard-sci-fi-strategy-that-i-know-a-player-will-want-to-use#post1421531\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So if my Leviathan is traveling at speed 6, aimed at the cololition ark, that is also traveling at speed six. If they fire railguns would the speed scale stack for damage?</div> </div> </div> </div>No. Storypath isn\u2019t a simulationist system in that way. You\u2019d resolve the attack as normal.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-03T17:44:57-08:00","id":1421704,"title":"","content":"Thank you you all for the comments and clarifications. In my game I think I am going to go with Mateus Luz suggestion of just one scale difference.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2421-cknight","name":"cKnight","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"47"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}